WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:04.540
Hey, David, do you believe that the number
of seats in the House of Representatives should

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.000
be expanded?

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.970
This came up on a recent youtube livestream
that I did.

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:10.950
Uh, and my answer is basically, yes, I do.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:14.500
Right now each house seat represents about
750,000 people.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:22.640
And uh, there have been 435 seats in the House
of Representatives dating all the way back

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.830
to the late twenties, I believe.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:30.029
1929 and obviously the population of the United
States has grown hugely.

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:37.149
I think it's almost three times bigger today
than it was back in 1929 maybe even more.

00:00:37.149 --> 00:00:42.589
I'm now just going by rough numbers, but the,
the point is each congressional district used

00:00:42.589 --> 00:00:47.479
to, uh, include way fewer people than it does
today.

00:00:47.479 --> 00:00:54.699
And if we wanted to keep the same proportional
representation that we had in 1929 today,

00:00:54.699 --> 00:01:00.339
we should grow the house of Representatives
to somewhere between 1100 and 1200 members.

00:01:00.339 --> 00:01:01.339
Okay.

00:01:01.339 --> 00:01:02.859
We have four 35.

00:01:02.859 --> 00:01:06.799
And what you have to understand when you think
about this issue is that this runs directly

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:10.009
counter to the interests of those who are
already in the House of Representatives.

00:01:10.009 --> 00:01:14.540
What I mean by that is if you got elected
to the House of Representatives and you currently

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:23.390
represent 750,000 people and you are one out
of 435, why would you want to see your power

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:27.960
diminished by expanding the number of seats
in the House of Representatives?

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:31.510
Because what you would effectively be doing
is you would reduce the number of people that

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:36.450
you represent by reducing the number of people
in each congressional district and you would

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:43.079
be voting to make yourself not one out of
100 and a one out of 435 you make yourself

00:01:43.079 --> 00:01:49.750
one out of a thousand or one out of 1200 and
most of the elected officials aren't going

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:52.249
to want to reduce their own power.

00:01:52.249 --> 00:01:54.310
It's just not something most people want to
do.

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:59.340
It's similar to campaign finance reform, and
I've talked about this before, when we ask

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:03.200
our elected officials to change the campaign
finance system.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:07.049
Yes, some of them say, I want to do it and
I would vote for it and I'll do it and I guess

00:02:07.049 --> 00:02:12.190
we believe them when they say that, but if
you were elected to begin with with a particular

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:18.799
campaign finance system, many of those people
are not going to want to take apart the system

00:02:18.799 --> 00:02:20.310
that got them elected to begin with.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:24.650
Now, there are people who are thinking this
through a little bit more critically and they

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:30.670
realize that if we change the entire system,
everybody benefits and maybe their party actually

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:34.409
benefits more, I would argue that Democrats
would benefit more from reforms to the campaign

00:02:34.409 --> 00:02:36.300
finance system than Republicans.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:39.860
Uh, and that's when you can actually get some
sort of partisan agreement.

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:40.860
Right.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:45.360
The reason that you would see significant
support for expanding the number of seats

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.920
in the House of Representatives would be if
one party determines that it would be good

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:49.920
for them.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.170
I believe that it would be better for Democrats.

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:53.890
Democrats would benefit more.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:58.860
When you expand the number of seats, you shrink
the advantage of the Electoral College for

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:01.410
Republicans currently that favors Republicans.

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:05.870
Um, and there are other sort of more micro
ways that I believe it would benefit Democrats.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:11.890
Uh, but to make a long story short, yes, we
absolutely should expand the number of seats

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:13.689
in the House of Representatives.

00:03:13.689 --> 00:03:14.700
Good luck doing it.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.720
Uh, significant opposition would be seen.

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:23.209
Um, definitely from Republicans, maybe even
from centrist Democrats as well.

00:03:23.209 --> 00:03:26.930
So I don't know that I see it happening anytime
soon, although I would love it.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:28.690
If you disagree with me, let me know.

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:29.690
I want to know why.

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:33.959
Why should we not expand the number of seats
in the House of Representatives?

00:03:33.959 --> 00:03:39.610
It used to expand with population and it is
not since 1929 what's so special.

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:40.610
Perfect.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:44.510
How about four 35 we've got a great bonus
show for you today.

